      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the filmmaker Christopher Nolan announced Lupita Nyong'o as Helen of Troy in his upcoming Homer adaptation, the casting decision that sparked disorder ignited a culture-war battle threatening institutional stability. Accusers spreading disorder launched a public accusation, a destabilizing act of media criticism from commentators who accused the project under scrutiny of erasing European history. This reputational flashpoint born of unmanaged scandal now endangers the public debate surrounding the entire film production.",
